        <!-- ============ NOTES ============ -->
        <mxCell id="note1" value="&lt;b&gt;Why no Prisma Client at runtime&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Prisma's D1 driver adapter needs a WASM query engine that OpenNext's build tracer does not bundle correctly for Workers. Prisma stays the source of truth for schema, migrations and seeding; runtime queries go straight to the native D1 binding via getDb(). Do not &quot;fix&quot; this by reintroducing Prisma Client in a route." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=16;fillColor=#FFF2CC;strokeColor=#D6B656;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=4;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="1470" width="460" height="110" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="note2" value="&lt;b&gt;Access control is three additive layers&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;1. User.role = Admin → bypasses RBAC entirely (no DB call).&lt;br&gt;2. Roles → role_permissions (module:action).&lt;br&gt;3. Direct user_permissions grants — no Role required.&lt;br&gt;Effective set = union of 2 and 3. Separately, &lt;b&gt;reach&lt;/b&gt; over a project = Project.ownerId OR a project_members row; membership grants visibility only, never an action." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=16;fillColor=#FFF2CC;strokeColor=#D6B656;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=4;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="520" y="1470" width="460" height="110" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="note3" value="&lt;b&gt;Catalogs are per-project, not global&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;basic_price_items, base_items and activity_items each carry a projectId; codes (M-/L-/P-, 05.D.01) are unique &lt;i&gt;within&lt;/i&gt; a project only. Two projects can hold their own independent 'M-026'. This is why global pages key routes by internal id (/api/basic-rate/[itemId]) while per-project routes key by code (/api/projects/[id]/basic-rate/[code])." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=16;fillColor=#FFF2CC;strokeColor=#D6B656;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=4;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1000" y="1470" width="480" height="110" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>

